  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it's good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S040",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's nice to meet you too, Doctor. I suppose what brings me in today is... well, it’s this whole situation with the local historical society. You see, I’ve been a member for years, mostly just attending the meetings and bringing a pie now and then, but recently they mentioned needing to raise funds for the old courthouse roof. And I just—I don't know, it was like a lightbulb went off, and suddenly I was taking on the entire fundraiser myself. I mean, I genuinely believed I could run the whole thing single-handedly. \n\nI started drawing up all these intricate quilt designs—because a raffle is always a good moneymaker, you know?—and I had fabric swatches spread out all over my dining room table, the living room floor, everywhere. Then I started calling all the volunteers, and I mean *all* of them, even people who hadn't been active in the society since the nineties. I was making these massive, color-coded schedules for everyone, assigning them tasks, and... and I was promising the board all these deadlines that, looking back now, I couldn't possibly meet. I told them we’d have three quilts done in a week and a fully catered gala planned by the end of the month. It was just... I was doing so much, and I felt like I had to do it all right that very second, and now it’s all just sort of crashed down on me.",
