    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "About how many days in a row did that unusually energized and irritable period last?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think back, because it all blends together when you're moving that fast, you know? I remember the leaves were just starting to turn when I first got the idea for the quilts, right around the time they put the pumpkins out at the grocery store. And then it just... it kept going. I was running on that high, just pushing and pushing through the holidays, through the new year, even into the early spring. So, goodness, that whole overdriven stretch with the historical society project went on for about five months, give or take. \n\nFive whole months of me just buzzing around like a bee trapped in a jar, making phone calls at all hours, reorganizing the fabric piles, arguing with Martha about the budget for the gala catering... I mean, I can hardly believe it went on that long when I sit here and say it out loud. But it did. Day in, day out, just this constant, humming energy and that terrible, prickly irritability every time someone couldn't match my pace. It wasn't until late March, maybe early April, that the bottom just completely fell out and everything fell apart. But for those five months, I was just... I was an absolute whirlwind, and I couldn't stop if I tried.",
